  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Numbers",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "Silver trumpets are used to call assemblies and to blow alarms—The cloud is taken from the tabernacle, and the children of Israel march forth in their prescribed order—The ark of the covenant goes before them in their journeyings.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And the Lord spake unto Moses, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:1",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "HEB hammered work."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:2",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And when they shall blow with them, all the assembly shall assemble themselves to thee at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 136,
            "text": "HEB tent of meeting."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:3",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And if they blow but with one trumpet, then the princes, which are heads of the thousands of Israel, shall gather themselves unto thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:4",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "When ye blow an alarm, then the camps that lie on the east parts shall go forward.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:5",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "When ye blow an alarm the second time, then the camps that lie on the south side shall take their journey: they shall blow an alarm for their journeys.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:6",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "But when the congregation is to be gathered together, ye shall blow, but ye shall not sound an alarm.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:7",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets; and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your generations.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "1 Chr. 15:24."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Chr. 15:24.",
            "prettyString": "1 Chronicles 15:24",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1chronicles",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 15,
                    "end": 15,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 24,
                        "end": 24
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:8",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And if ye go to war in your land against the enemy that oppresseth you, then ye shall blow an alarm with the trumpets; and ye shall be remembered before the Lord your God, and ye shall be saved from your enemies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 10:9",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Also in the day of your gladness, and in your solemn days, and in the beginnings of your months, ye shall blow with the trumpets over your burnt offerings, and over the sacrifices of your peace offerings; that they may be to you for a memorial before your God: I am the Lord your God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "HEB appointed feast days."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "Lev. 23:24; Ps. 81:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
